    {
      "diff": "@@ -29,18 +29,17 @@ wsbuglink:17779[]\n \n === Bug Fixes\n \n-The following vulnerabilities have been fixed:\n+// The following vulnerabilities have been fixed:\n \n-* wssalink:2022-06[]\n-F5 Ethernet Trailer dissector infinite loop.\n-wsbuglink:18307[].\n+// * wssalink:2022-07[]\n+// Foo dissector {crash,infinite loop,memory leak}.\n+// wsbuglink:xxxxx[].\n // cveidlink:2022-xxxx[].\n-// Fixed in master: 67326401a5\n-// Fixed in release-3.6: 68c3d706c7\n-// Fixed in release-3.4: 0664b90b35\n+// Fixed in master: xxxxx\n+// Fixed in release-3.6: xxxxx\n+// Fixed in release-3.4: xxxxx\n // CVSS AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:L\n-// CWE-835\n-// * f5ethtrailer: Infinite loop in legacy style dissector. wsbuglink:18307[].\n+// CWE-???\n \n The following bugs have been fixed:\n \n@@ -49,34 +48,6 @@ The following bugs have been fixed:\n //* cveidlink:2014-2486[]\n //* Wireshark keeps banging out random chords on your piano and yelling “LIPS LIKE SUGUAR, SUGAR KISSES” because it was funny that one time at a party.\n \n-* TCAP Malformed exception on externally re-assembled packet wsbuglink:10515[].\n-\n-* Extended 3GPP-GPRS-Negotiated-QoS-profile strings decoded incompletely wsbuglink:10688[].\n-\n-* HTTP2 dissector decodes first SSL record only wsbuglink:11173[].\n-\n-* L2TP improvements - cookie length detection, UDP encapsulation and more wsbuglink:16565[].\n-\n-* USB Truncation of URB_isochronous in frames wsbuglink:18021[].\n-\n-* ISUP/BICC parameter summary text duplication wsbuglink:18094[].\n-\n-* Running rpm-setup.sh shows missing packages that Centos does not need wsbuglink:18166[].\n-\n-* IPX/IPX RIP: Crash on expand subtree wsbuglink:18234[].\n-\n-* Qt: A file or packet comment that is too large will corrupt the pcapng file wsbuglink:18235[].\n-\n-* BGP dissector bug wsbuglink:18248[].\n-\n-* Wrong interpretation of the cbsp.rep_period field in epan/dissectors/packet-gsm_cbsp.c wsbuglink:18254[].\n-\n-* Assertion due to incorrect mask for btatt.battery_power_state.* wsbuglink:18267[].\n-\n-* Qt: Expert Info dialog not showing Malformed Frame when Frame length is less than captured length wsbuglink:18312[].\n-\n-* Wireshark and tshark become non-responsive when reading certain packets wsbuglink:18313[].\n-\n === New and Updated Features\n \n // === Removed Features and Support\n@@ -93,33 +64,15 @@ There are no new protocols in this release.\n // ag -A1 '(define PSNAME|proto_register_protocol[^_])' $(git diff --name-only v3.4.9.. | ag packet- | sort -u)\n [commaize]\n --\n-BGP\n-BICC\n-BT ATT\n-CBSP\n-Couchbase\n-F5 Ethernet Trailer\n-Frame\n-GTP\n-GTP (prime)\n-IPsec\n-ISUP\n-L2TP\n-NAS-5GS\n-Protobuf\n-SCCP\n-TCP\n-TLS\n --\n \n === New and Updated Capture File Support\n \n-// There is no new or updated capture file support in this release.\n+There is no new or updated capture file support in this release.\n // Add one file type per line between the -- delimiters.\n-[commaize]\n---\n-pcap, pcapng\n---\n+// [commaize]\n+// --\n+// --\n \n === New File Format Decoding Support\n \n",
      "collapsed": false,
